{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/794543-solo-newbie-vtr-with-a-gm-emulator","id":794543,"title":"Solo: Newbie VTR with a GM Emulator","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-28T19:06:56-08:00","id":794543,"title":"Solo: Newbie VTR with a GM Emulator","content":"Hi All,<br /> <br /> I'm new to all things Darkness and VTR, naturally. I'm usually more of a cosmic horror person, but I've recently decided to look into this stuff, and am rather surprised at how much I'm enjoying the ride.<br /> I've a soft spot for what some people call solo roleplaying. The general idea is that folks use products such as the Mythic GameMaster Emulator to take the place of a GM, and basically inject unpredictability into a &quot;session.&quot; It might be somewhat more like a writing exercise than anything else, but is still potentially fun, personally speaking.<br /> So, I was thinking that I would love to try chronicling the experiences of someone newly embraced, as a sort of Learning experience for VTR, and for personal enjoyment.<br /> I'm not sure what direction it might ultimately take, but just to begin, what might happen if someone were more or less abandoned by their sire after embrace? There is probably no &quot;vampiric foundlings society,&quot; so to speak, and I imagine the first few nights are going to be hell, especially if the embraced has no idea what's happened.<br /> <br /> More generally, I was wondering if anybody here had experience running a chronicle solo, in this fashion. I know Mythic has been mentioned here a couple of times. I wonder if I' better off just starting with a more conventional neonate, but something about the raw terror of those first few nights is weirdly appealing.<br /> Any ideas on one or both of these questions would be greatly appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10499-caplin","name":"Caplin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T00:31:44-08:00","id":794662,"title":"","content":"Not really on topic, but it should probably be pointed out: The origina VtR demo adventure was about just such an event. The PC coterie woke up in an alley, now turned into vampires. Wat do?<br /> Check it out here: <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full?term=vampire+requiem+demo&amp;it=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/...uiem+demo&amp;it=1</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T06:08:16-08:00","id":794782,"title":"","content":"If you have second edition, take a look at the Larva rules. Basically, they are the new 'accidental embraces' of the game line. Sometimes if a person is fully exsanguinated, they will come back as a Clanless vampire with some harsh flaws that normal vampires don't get. They can eventually be uplifted into a normal clan either by finding a mentor, or by diablerie. But - such a character would have an interesting time when they come back from the dead - dealing with the beast, its urges, the powers of vitae, etc.<br /> <br /> There are a number of easy hooks that will get the character on the radar of other Kindred:<ul><li>Heightened Blood Sympathy gives them tools to find their accidental Sire.</li> <li>Bending or breaking the Masquerade will get them Invictus (Conspiracy of Silence) attention.</li> <li>Feeding in established feeding grounds might get them discovered by a Regent.</li> <li>Coming across another Kindred anywhere will have their beasts recognize each other (unless obfuscate is up).</li> <li>The Cacophony might catch wind of them and reveal the character to those with the savvy to understand the signs.</li> </ul>I haven't checked out the Mythic tool you mention, but it sounds interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T07:08:23-08:00","id":794801,"title":"","content":"Holy Means Revenants, not Larvae, two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:02:39-08:00","id":794910,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the info. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been snapping up mostly first edition stuff so far, though I guess I should look into second\u2014from what I've read, some of the story-focused bits, like touchstones, might fit in very well with the solo RP idea.<br /> <br /> I also love the stuff in Damnation City, though the trouble with solo is always figuring out where prep stops and the game begins. I want to leave plenty of room to be surprised.<br /> <br /> One more question, if I may\u2026 I've been thinking lately that winter is probably a vampire's favorite season. I live near Seattle, and we don't seem to see the sun all that often. How much would the Beast mind a super overcast day? As a totally blind person, I only really notice the sun when it's shining enough to warm the skin. Somehow I think that's a bit too much for vampires. On the other hand, if sunset is around 4:30 or so, that's a lot more time for the Kindred to be active. I guess this might very well be &quot;it varies,&quot; territory.<br /> <br /> As always, any thoughts on these questions are appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10499,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10499-caplin","user":"Caplin","date":".  formatting. 12-29-2015, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10499-caplin","name":"Caplin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T10:25:57-08:00","id":794924,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, while it is true that the sun is down longer in Winter, people also tend to be somewhat less active, especially when it is very cold outside, which for some Kindred might make hunting slightly harder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:03:55-08:00","id":794955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/794543-solo-newbie-vtr-with-a-gm-emulator?p=794924#post794924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind, while it is true that the sun is down longer in Winter, people also tend to be somewhat less active, especially when it is very cold outside, which for some Kindred might make hunting slightly harder.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. I failed to consider that aspect. New Year's Eve, on the other hand, might be an ideal time, what with all the parties going on and all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10499-caplin","name":"Caplin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T11:06:49-08:00","id":794958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caplin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/794543-solo-newbie-vtr-with-a-gm-emulator?p=794910#post794910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the info. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been snapping up mostly first edition stuff so far, though I guess I should look into second\u2014from what I've read, some of the story-focused bits, like touchstones, might fit in very well with the solo RP idea.<br /> <br /> I also love the stuff in Damnation City, though the trouble with solo is always figuring out where prep stops and the game begins. I want to leave plenty of room to be surprised.<br /> <br /> One more question, if I may\u2026 I've been thinking lately that winter is probably a vampire's favorite season. I live near Seattle, and we don't seem to see the sun all that often. How much would the Beast mind a super overcast day? As a totally blind person, I only really notice the sun when it's shining enough to warm the skin. Somehow I think that's a bit too much for vampires. On the other hand, if sunset is around 4:30 or so, that's a lot more time for the Kindred to be active. I guess this might very well be &amp;quot;it varies,&amp;quot; territory.<br /> <br /> As always, any thoughts on these questions are appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, most vampires would be in day sleep during the time the sun is up, whether it's overcast or not. Remaining awake during the day is possible, but it takes a significant effort and the vampire risks falling asleep pretty much at any time. The Ordo Dracul have techniques to get around this, though (Second Tier of Coil of Banes in first edition, or the Day Wake Conditioning Scale in second edition).<br /> <br /> For those who do manage to stay up during the day, I don't think cloud cover would normally be enough to keep them from taking damage. In first edition, the third tier of Coil of Banes prevents the vampire from taking sunlight damage in twilight conditions, like the early morning, late evening, or when it's extremely overcast.<br /> <br /> In second edition, sunlight damage is a bit more variable. Vampires take more damage from sunlight the lower their Humanity is, and they take the damage at shorter intervals the higher their Blood Potency is. Covering up so that your skin isn't exposed can lower a vampire's effective Blood Potency by 1 for the purposes of calculating sunlight damage. I would probably rule that overcast conditions would have the same effect as the vampire covering her skin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}